(a) The traffic-control devices listed below shall be designated as follows:
(1) The mayor and city council shall, by ordinance, after engineering and traffic investigations, designate the any of the following:
a. Speed zones;
b. Through highways;
c. One-way streets and other directional control devices;
d. Freight loading zones and regulations;
e. Parking and no-parking zones and regulations thereon;
f. Stop signals and other traffic signals;
g. Taxicab zones;
h. Particularly dangerous railroad grade crossings;
i. Speed reduction mechanisms; and
j. Any other sign, marking or zone necessary for orderly and safe conditions on the streets of the City of Oakwood.
(2) The manager, or his/her designee, after the completion of a traffic engineering study and analysis, shall administratively approve the installation of any traffic control devices if warranted by the standards set forth by the Manual of Uniform Traffic Control Devices adopted by the state transportation board.
(b) The manager, or his/her designee, shall maintain or cause to be recorded a current schedule of all approved traffic control devices, which record shall be available for inspection by the public at City Hall.
(c) All traffic-control devices shall conform to specifications in the Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices adopted by the state transportation board. All signs and signals required hereunder for a particular purpose shall, so far as practicable, be uniform as to type and location throughout the City of Oakwood. All traffic-control devices so erected, when consistent with state law and this Code, shall be official traffic-control devices of the City of Oakwood.
(d) Any violation of any traffic zone, marking, sign or other traffic-control device established hereunder shall be a violation of this Code pursuant to Code Section 1-11.
(Ord. No. 2019-CO-09-793, § 1, 10-14-2019)

